.TH CRUNCH_MQ_OPEN 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
crunch_mq_open \- Linux x86-64 syscall 240
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int crunch_mq_open(const char* name, int flags, mode_t mode, const struct crunch_mq_attr* attributes);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes raw mq_open. Unlike the POSIX libc wrapper, the kernel queue name must omit its leading slash.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mq_open (2)
